 equivalent to $R.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(T∨R)∧T & ≡T∧(T∨R) \\\\  & ≡T≢R.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $R.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R∧(T∨R) & ≡R∧(R∨T) \\\\  & ≡R.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $R.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(R∨T)∧R & ≡R∧(R∨T) \\\\  & ≡R.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572669 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d4ea352-2a82-5ff5-8c08-b7f9a09929e6" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Disjunction Absorbs Conjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d5d890b-dbff-54dd-8714-164a761eead1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572351} {:answer/id #uuid "5e53d921-3fb4-5f74-bff7-edc72cf430f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572430} {:answer/id #uuid "b5ad27c1-d176-56fd-a3a6-de2511186a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572518} {:answer/id #uuid "bd33bebd-120b-5f91-a1b4-e6c583d8f143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572527} {:answer/id #uuid "f641586b-a1ac-55b7-9450-73e0e253da93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5ad27c1-d176-56fd-a3a6-de2511186a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572518} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ad0f25f-fa4f-57f8-bd2a-9b8d93bbc416" :answer-field/key "selection" 